# Simpler Collection Iteration

The **foreach** loop is designed to run through every element in an array or collection without worrying about indices.

```csharp
foreach (Type variable in collection)
{
    // use variable
}
```

Example:
```csharp
string[] names = { "Mario", "Luigi", "Peach" };
foreach (string name in names)
{
    Debug.Log(name);
}
```

**Pros**: Cleaner, no index to manage. **Cons**: Cannot modify the collection while iterating, and you can't easily get the index (unless you use a counter).

